## 2. Family arithmetic (own math from shipped `web/static/css/tailwind.css`
   RGB values, WCAG relative-luminance formula, cross-validated against a
   real render — see below)

  solid gray-800, dark:text-gray-400          → 5.78:1  PASS (matches X8.2's own number)
  solid gray-700, dark:text-gray-400          → 4.06:1  FAILS 4.5 → escalation to gray-300 required
  solid gray-700, dark:text-gray-300          → 6.995:1 PASS — confirmed live-render via
    getComputedStyle (bg rgb(55,65,81) exact gray-700, color rgb(209,213,219)
    exact gray-300) AND raw PNG pixel sampling of explorer.html's date-range
    buttons in dark mode — sampled background pixel (55,65,81) exact match,
    peak text pixel ≈(204,208,214) vs gray-300 (209,213,219), confirms 6.995:1
    for real
  dark:bg-gray-700/50-in-gray-800 (rate-assumptions.html glide-path box),
    dark:text-gray-400                        → 4.88:1  PASS, correctly NOT escalated
  opacity-60 box (own bg-gray-800 nested in bg-gray-800 card; CSS `opacity`
    blends the WHOLE box incl. text with the ancestor backdrop, not just the
    fill):
      dark:text-gray-400  → 3.03:1  FAILS → escalation required
      dark:text-gray-300  → 4.57:1  PASSES (barely) — matches attempt 3's
        choice in bigticket-card.html/expense-sources-list.html/
        income-sources-list.html (3 of the 9 gray-300 escalations)
  opacity-50 row (explorer.html suppressed-duplicate rows — the disclosed
    residual, see #4 below)
  large-text case: insights.html:189/222 `text-2xl font-bold` "$0.00" on
    solid gray-800 → same 5.78:1 as the solid-gray-800 family, clears both
    3:1 and 4.5:1 comfortably.

Spot-checked all 9 gray-300 escalations by category (3 opacity-60 boxes:
bigticket-card/expense-sources-list/income-sources-list; 3 gray-700-surface
sites: healthcare-person.html's "Coverage Timeline" captions, confirmed via
template read that the enclosing card is `bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-700`
solid, not gray-800; 3 opacity-50 rows: explorer.html, the disclosed
residual). All 9 check out — correct family, correct color, correct math.

IMPORTANT CORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST AXE PASS: my first live axe run showed
21 `color-contrast` violations on `/dashboard#dark` that did not match my
hand math (axe reported background colors like `#523e4f`/`#384a50` that
match NEITHER `getComputedStyle` NOR real rendered pixels). Root cause: my
harness set `localStorage`+`class="dark"` via JS on an already-painted LIGHT
page and ran axe immediately, catching Tailwind's `transition-colors
duration-200` mid-transition. Fixed by reloading after setting the theme (so
the real inline head-script at `base.html:20-27` sets the class BEFORE first
paint, exactly like a real user re-visiting with the cookie already set —
zero transition). After the fix: 0 color-contrast violations on
`/dashboard#dark`, 0 attributable ones on `/explorer#dark` (see #5).
Independently re-verified the corrected numbers three ways (WCAG formula
math from shipped CSS values, `getComputedStyle` on the live dark DOM, and
raw PNG pixel sampling of screenshots) — all three agree to within rounding
for every site checked (kpis.html's rose-900/20 caption: 6.64:1 sampled vs
6.62:1 computed; dashboard-verdict-bar's emerald-900/20 caption: matches;
explorer's solid-gray-700 button: matches).

