## Verdict

Attempt 3 completed the grep-driven completion sweep correctly: exactly 4
legitimate exemptions remain, all 97 gray-400 fixes and all 9 gray-300
escalations check out against real math AND a real render (including a
correction I had to make to my own harness, documented above, which
resolved to zero net regressions), the delta is scope-clean across every
file sampled, the one disclosed residual is honestly reported with correct
numbers and appropriately out of this attempt's declared scope, and the
build/test/render pipeline is fully green. PASS.

## Observations (non-blocking, for the lead)

- FINDING (not a FAIL): explorer.html's suppressed-duplicate rows remain
  non-conformant under WCAG 1.4.3 because `opacity-50` sits on the `<tr>`
  rather than being expressed as a background-only/icon-based suppression
  cue; recommend a follow-up task scoped to restructure that specific
  pattern (not a token swap).
- Pre-existing, byte-identical-to-master, out of X8's scope: kpis.html's
  `text-emerald-600/500` light-mode captions (10 axe nodes); explorer.html's
  JS-driven active-button `bg-indigo-600`/white (4.46:1, just under
  threshold); missing accessible names on 3 `<select>` elements across
  dashboard/explorer (WCAG 4.1.2 / ACCESSIBILITY.md point 4); monte-
  carlo.html's decorative svg still lacking `aria-hidden="true"` (repeated
  from X8.1/X8.2's own observations, still unaddressed, still out of scope).
- Tooling note for future a11y checkers: setting `class="dark"` via JS on an
  already-painted page and running axe immediately can catch Tailwind
  `transition-colors` mid-flight and produce false-positive color-contrast
  violations with background colors that match neither `getComputedStyle`
  nor real pixels. Always reload after setting the theme so the real
  head-inline script (`base.html:20-27`) sets the class pre-paint, or
  disable transitions, before trusting an axe dark-mode run.
